From fb46148e52249d4e8f1b6fd780ad96053c9b48c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mitzev <ogi@kunasystems.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 23:23:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/42] Parser: class keyword + class-body attribute acceptance

Teaches the parser to recognize `class` as a weak keyword that desugars
to a #[repr(cpp)] struct plus an inherent impl with any body methods as
members. Extends single-inheritance parsing (`class D : B { ... }`) and
relaxes attribute gating so class fields accept #[doc] / #[cfg] / etc.
AST validation learns the new shape; stability lowering recognizes the
fork ABIs as accepted extern strings.
---
